{
  "id": "situation-counter",
  "title": "Situation counter",
  "summary": "Spot and count one camera situation, like a pot boiling over or a dog licking itself.",
  "category": "run",
  "capability_ids": [
    "v1.watches",
    "v1.camera",
    "v1.interactions"
  ],
  "support": {
    "source_api_revision": 71,
    "tested_contract_api_revision": 71,
    "minimum_recipe_api_revision": 71,
    "released": "unknown; compare public changes and installed health",
    "installed": "unknown",
    "ready": null,
    "requirements": "GET /v1/health, /v1/capabilities and installed /v1/guide must confirm every operation and grant, and the installed API revision must be at least 71 (situation in POST /v1/watches). Source support alone is insufficient."
  },
  "execution": {
    "phone": [
      "Timer → camera → free local change check → Clef yes/no on changed photos → episode tally on the phone → watch.matched event and, for alert situations, an urgent owner notice.",
      "The phone expands situation into the tuned question, the tally (track = the situation id, or \"situation\" for own words) and the alert rule; unchanged photos reuse the last answer for free."
    ],
    "controller": [
      "Optional: read GET /v1/watches/{id}/tally to archive day totals; the card and the count work with no agent.",
      "Pick the situation with the owner: a library id from GET /v1/situations or the owner's own words."
    ],
    "server": "Only Clef photo checks leave the phone (model left out, so Clef is the default for a camera watch); direct or relay transport still requires a running reachable phone."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "A count is sampled photos judged by a model, not continuous coverage or proof: gaps, a locked camera or the thing being out of frame are unknown, not zero.",
    "It does not diagnose health or detect fire: a smoke or boiling-over count is a nudge, not a safety alarm."
  ],
  "lifecycle": {
    "start": "POST /v1/watches with the start example; retain the returned watch_id. Then render/post the card with resource_id.",
    "update": "GET /v1/watches/{id}/tally first. To change the situation or timing, archive the tally, DELETE the old watch, POST the revised body. No watch PATCH exists.",
    "pause": "POST /v1/watches/{id}/pause with {\"paused\":true}; resume with false. Confirm user_paused from the returned metadata. Expiry is unchanged.",
    "stop": "DELETE /v1/watches/{id}; confirm deleted equals the saved id and watch.ended reason deleted. Archive needed tally BEFORE deletion. Cancel the interaction separately."
  },
  "failure": [
    "Own words that look like an id (lowercase_with_underscores) but aren't in the library are refused: describe it with spaces instead.",
    "A busy or locked camera is a gap; poor light, glare and odd angles cause misses and false counts. Aim the camera and try a known example first."
  ],
  "cost": [
    "Clef photo checks from the phone's model budget: at most max_paid_per_hour (30 here, under the 50-an-hour limit some phones have) an hour; unchanged pictures reuse the last answer for free. Read GET /v1/limits and lower the cap or lengthen interval_s for long runs."
  ],
  "extensions": [
    "Send {\"situation\": {\"describe\": \"...\", \"alert\": true}} to count own words and notify the owner when one starts.",
    "Add callback_when on the situation id, or rules, to reach a controller or show other notices; min and count_only_while tune what counts."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/v1/watches",
        "body": {
          "situation": "pot_boiling_over",
          "data": [
            "camera"
          ],
          "camera": "rear",
          "interval_s": 20,
          "expires_in_s": 7776000,
          "max_paid_per_hour": 30,
          "local": {
            "change_check": true,
            "sensitivity": "normal",
            "max_reuse_s": 300
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "watch_id": "wsituation01",
          "label": "Pot boiling over",
          "user_paused": false,
          "created_at": "2026-11-04T10:00:00Z",
          "expires_at": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z",
          "interval_s": 20,
          "data": [
            "camera"
          ],
          "checks": 0,
          "matches": 0,
          "last_match_at": null,
          "readings_held": 0,
          "last_check": null,
          "usage": {
            "model": "clef",
            "answered_locally": 0,
            "paid_calls": 0,
